Third-party engines and models
------------------------------
Bundled or downloaded engines, patches under external/patches/, Seed-VC
compatibility excerpts (see backend/app/fixtures/COPYING.seed-vc), FFmpeg
builds, and model weights (including YuE2 weights under CC BY-NC where
applicable) have their own licenses. Review those artifacts before redistribution
or commercial use.

Attribution for planned / inspired work
---------------------------------------
- Voice-profile UX pattern inspired by LocalAI (MIT) — https://github.com/mudler/LocalAI
  OpenFabric implements its own FastAPI + SQLite voice-profile store; LocalAI code is not copied.
- Talking / audiobook engine: GPT-SoVITS (MIT) — https://github.com/RVC-Boss/GPT-SoVITS
  Not bundled; optional install via OPENFABRIC_GPT_SOVITS_DIR. OpenFabric never
  auto-downloads pretrained weights. Singing voice cloning remains Seed-VC.
  Do not use AGPL VoiceStudio code.
- Audiobook options (pasted text, TXT, and EPUB import, pronunciation map, per-chapter regenerate, MP3 and chaptered M4B export) were inspired by Pandrator (MIT, https://github.com/lukaszliniewicz/Pandrator). OpenFabric reimplemented them in its own code; Pandrator source is not copied or vendored.
- macOS ad-hoc signing for Electron downloads (identity "-", hardenedRuntime false, CI codesign verify, Open Anyway docs) follows the pattern from inikolax/remiqora v0.2.2 commit bd8316e / issue #33 (MIT). OpenFabric reimplemented the same electron-builder and workflow checks; Remiqora application code was not vendored for this change.
- Tagged downloads keep a reusable artist name and an optional album, and YuE generations store the song title apart from style tags. Those ideas follow Remiqora 0.2.2 (MIT, https://github.com/inikolax/remiqora). OpenFabric reimplemented them; Remiqora application code was not copied.
- Audiobook chapter-audio cache, cue sheets, language readiness, and collection ZIP manifests were inspired by audiobook tools such as Pandrator (MIT, https://github.com/lukaszliniewicz/Pandrator). OpenFabric reimplemented them. VoiceStudio (AGPL) code was not copied.
- Pause-aware narration uses local PCM energy so a long chapter is not cut through a loud region. Parakeet and other VAD weights were not downloaded; their weight license was not treated as cleared for this app.
